<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116169" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠμάδιος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠμός</span>) as epith. of Dionysus,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠμηστής</span>
			, because he had <i>human sacrifices</i> at Chios and
			Tenedos, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>H.</u>
				30.5
			</span></i>, Euelp. ap.<i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Abst.</u>
				2.55
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠ. χοροί</span> dances in his
			honour, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				14.2138
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>raw,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρέα</span> Epic. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Arch.Pap.</u>
				7p.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦμος</span>) <i>passing over the shoulder,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεβρίς, τελαμών,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				1.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				13.308
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
